+    <div class="docs-meta"><span>Receiver trust and maritime</span><a href="https://github.com/ashfordeOU/kshana/blob/main/docs/ADAPTERS.md">Edit on GitHub</a><span>Source: <code>docs/ADAPTERS.md</code></span></div>
+    <div class="prose"><h1 id="adapters-new-devices-and-formats-without-engine-changes">Adapters: new devices and formats without engine changes</h1>
+<p>An adapter teaches Kshana to read a device&#39;s or a logger&#39;s export, by configuration only. Each one is a
+folder under <a href="https://github.com/ashfordeOU/kshana/blob/main/adapters"><code>adapters/</code></a> that the registry checks on every change.</p>
+<pre data-lang="shell"><code class="hljs language-bash">kshana connect adapters list adapters      <span class="hljs-comment"># the adapters that pass</span>
+kshana connect adapters check adapters     <span class="hljs-comment"># validate every manifest and run every vector; exit 1 on any failure</span></code></pre>
+<h2 id="what-an-adapter-holds">What an adapter holds<a class="anchor" href="#what-an-adapter-holds" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<pre data-lang="text"><code class="hljs">adapters/&lt;name&gt;/
+  adapter.toml        the manifest (below)
+  &lt;name&gt;.connect.toml the kshana.connect/1 mapping file (docs/CONNECT.md)
+  sample.csv          a sample log you may share: no customer data, no personal data
+  vector.toml         a conformance vector: the sample, the mapping, a station, the expected output
+  expected.obs.jsonl  the kshana.obs/1 records the mapping must give, byte for byte</code></pre>
+<p>The files may also live elsewhere in the repository; the manifest&#39;s paths are relative to it. The
+bundled examples point at <code>examples/connect/</code> and <code>conformance/connect/</code>.</p>
+<pre data-lang="toml"><code class="hljs language-ini"><span class="hljs-attr">schema</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;kshana.adapter/1&quot;</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">name</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;timing-monitor&quot;</span>                  <span class="hljs-comment"># lower-case letters, digits and -; unique</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">title</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;A timing receiver&#x27;s monitoring export (...)&quot;</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">kind</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;mapping&quot;</span>                         <span class="hljs-comment"># the only kind so far</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">mapping</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;timing-monitor.connect.toml&quot;</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">vector</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;vector.toml&quot;</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">maintainer</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;Your name or organisation&quot;</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">licence</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;AGPL-3.0-only&quot;</span>                <span class="hljs-comment"># SPDX id of the adapter&#x27;s files</span>
+<span class="hljs-attr">status</span> = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;community&quot;</span>                     <span class="hljs-comment"># example | community | maintained</span>
+<span class="hljs-comment"># reference = &quot;https://...&quot;              # the format&#x27;s public documentation, if any</span></code></pre>
+<h2 id="what-the-check-refuses">What the check refuses<a class="anchor" href="#what-the-check-refuses" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<ul>
+<li>A manifest that does not parse, has an unknown field, the wrong <code>schema</code>, a bad <code>name</code>, <code>kind</code> or
+<code>status</code>, or an empty <code>title</code>, <code>maintainer</code> or <code>licence</code>.</li>
+<li>A mapping file that does not load.</li>
+<li>A vector that does not run, that uses a mapping other than the adapter&#39;s own, or whose output differs
+from its expected file (the first differing line is named).</li>
+<li>Two adapters with the same name.</li>
+</ul>
+<p><code>tests/adapters.rs</code> runs the check on the registry and on deliberately broken adapters, one for each
+refusal above.</p>
+<h2 id="writing-one">Writing one<a class="anchor" href="#writing-one" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<ol>
+<li>Write the mapping for your export (<code>docs/CONNECT.md</code>), and try it:
+<code>kshana connect map sample.csv --mapping &lt;name&gt;.connect.toml --station station.toml</code>.</li>
+<li>Write the vector and record its expected output:
+<code>kshana connect check vector.toml --bless</code>. Read the output before you commit it.</li>
+<li>Write <code>adapter.toml</code>, then run <code>kshana connect adapters check adapters</code>.</li>
+<li>Open a pull request with the folder, using the &quot;Adapter submission&quot; issue template if you want to
+discuss it first. Contributions are licensed as <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code> describes, with signed-off
+commits.</li>
+</ol>
+<h2 id="planned">Planned<a class="anchor" href="#planned" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<p>Runtime plug-ins (WebAssembly or Python) for formats a mapping cannot express, on the same manifest
+with a new <code>kind</code>. Binary formats are read by built-in readers today (<code>kshana obs convert</code>).</p>
+</div>
