+
+# Adapters: new devices and formats without engine changes
+
+An adapter teaches Kshana to read a device's or a logger's export, by configuration only. Each one is a folder under adapters/ that the registry checks on every change.
+
+```
+kshana connect adapters list adapters      # the adapters that pass
+kshana connect adapters check adapters     # validate every manifest and run every vector; exit 1 on any failure
+```
+
+## What an adapter holds#
+
+```
+adapters/<name>/
+adapter.toml        the manifest (below)
+<name>.connect.toml the kshana.connect/1 mapping file (docs/CONNECT.md)
+sample.csv          a sample log you may share: no customer data, no personal data
+vector.toml         a conformance vector: the sample, the mapping, a station, the expected output
+expected.obs.jsonl  the kshana.obs/1 records the mapping must give, byte for byte
+```
+
+The files may also live elsewhere in the repository; the manifest's paths are relative to it. The bundled examples point at examples/connect/ and conformance/connect/.
+
+```
+schema = "kshana.adapter/1"
+name = "timing-monitor"                  # lower-case letters, digits and -; unique
+title = "A timing receiver's monitoring export (...)"
+kind = "mapping"                         # the only kind so far
+mapping = "timing-monitor.connect.toml"
+vector = "vector.toml"
+maintainer = "Your name or organisation"
+licence = "AGPL-3.0-only"                # SPDX id of the adapter's files
+status = "community"                     # example | community | maintained
+# reference = "https://..."              # the format's public documentation, if any
+```
+
+## What the check refuses#
+
+- A manifest that does not parse, has an unknown field, the wrong schema, a bad name, kind or status, or an empty title, maintainer or licence.
+
+- A mapping file that does not load.
+
+- A vector that does not run, that uses a mapping other than the adapter's own, or whose output differs from its expected file (the first differing line is named).
+
+- Two adapters with the same name.
+
+tests/adapters.rs runs the check on the registry and on deliberately broken adapters, one for each refusal above.
+
+## Writing one#
+
+- Write the mapping for your export (docs/CONNECT.md), and try it: kshana connect map sample.csv --mapping <name>.connect.toml --station station.toml.
+
+- Write the vector and record its expected output: kshana connect check vector.toml --bless. Read the output before you commit it.
+
+- Write adapter.toml, then run kshana connect adapters check adapters.
+
+- Open a pull request with the folder, using the "Adapter submission" issue template if you want to discuss it first. Contributions are licensed as CONTRIBUTING.md describes, with signed-off commits.
+
+## Planned#
+
+Runtime plug-ins (WebAssembly or Python) for formats a mapping cannot express, on the same manifest with a new kind. Binary formats are read by built-in readers today (kshana obs convert).
+
